we begin with an update now from the  i-team a valley family calling for  answers tonight in their son's death the  unlv student was taken to sunrise  hospital last week after collapsing at a  fraternity boxing match his family tells  us he could not survive those severe  brain injuries it is a story the i-team  broke first here on 8 news now vanessa  murphy continues her coverage this  evening  nathan valencia's family and attorney  say a fraternity boxing match held here  at the sahara event center cost the  student his life they tell the i-team he  was a healthy 20-year-old who  participated for charity and they  believe a lack of precautions taken at  the event led to his death it should  have been done correctly it shouldn't  have been overlooked to lose someone so  precious like that it's hard xavier dela  rosa says he's known nathan valencia  since their days at bishop gorman high  school nathan then moving on to unlv and  becoming a member of sigma alpha epsilon  [Music]  on november 19th he participated in this  boxing match held by another unlv  fraternity kappa sigma he collapsed  after the fight  a family attorney tells the i-team no  medical help was immediately available  and it appears there was no professional  referee a formal statement from the  family and their legal team reads in  part college students should not be  placed in a situation where they are  pitted against each other for combat  kappa sigma fight night is an event that  has been held annually and was well  known to both unlv and the national  kappa sigma fraternity a spokesman for  unlv tells the i-team the university is  actively looking into the incident like  this this thing  it's like an underground fight club joe  castro is a friend of nathan's who was  there event itself didn't seem very  organized but i saw no medical medic  no doctors no nothing we reached out to  the kappa sigma fraternity and we  received a statement about condolences  for nathan's family and the unlv  community we also reached out to the  sahara event center they also sent a  statement about condolences the family's  attorney tells me metro police are  investigating reporting in las vegas  vanessa murphy live local now  unlv's president dr keith whitfield sent  the campus community a message about  nathan valencia's death earlier today we  have that along with complete statements  and the link to a gofundme for medical  and funeral expenses it's all on our  website at 8newsnow.com
 

